/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (         Through a series of meetings with TF, we focused on identifying where support was most needed and which components of the model were not yet functional. This process highlighted four key problem areas: \(1\) inadequate data visualisation, \(2\) missing vulnerability functions for new hazards, \(3\) a non-functional network construction pipeline, and \(4\) incomplete calculation of GDP losses.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (           Although previous interns had produced code to generate the power network and visualise GDP exposure, it was not documented and difficult to extend. Team 1 therefore decided to rebuild the component from scratch, allowing us to develop a clear understanding of the model and produce an implementation that could be explained, maintained, and built upon going forward. TF were initially somewhat unclear about the nuances of this task, and so our meetings were mostly structured in a semi-informal sense. We raised questions and discussed all points of clarification, showing any working code with them. Over time it became much more clear what the end result would look like.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
