260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 751 0 R
/E (Using GDP or GDP per capita would yield different results for our model. Both sources of data were associated with regions \(regional GDP, vs regional GDP per capita\). GDP regions were smaller and more numerous, and therefore more precise, than GDP per capita data. However, attributing GDP data to targets is a longer process. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 752 0 R
/E (We discussed with TF to see which was the preferred method. Using GDP per capita and multiplying by target population was concluded to be computationally simpler than the alternative. \(Using GDP data, counting total population in a given region, dividing GDP by population, then multiplying said GDP per capita by each targets population.\))
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
262 0 obj
<<
