/S /P
/P 754 0 R
/E (The method we ended up using was using regional gdp per capita data, and multiplying by target populations to find individual target gdp. As mentioned earlier, this was to reduce computational complexity/load.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 755 0 R
/E (Methodology lacks transmission line electricity allocation. The base methodology only allocates electricity demand to targets; electricity flowing through transmission lines is not calculated. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9 10]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 756 0 R
/E (We created new code to calculate electricity pathing from powerplants to targets - two methods were used. Method 1\) Assume each target only consumes from one powerplant, calculate the combination of target-power plant links needed to provide power to all targets. Method 2\) Each target consumes from the closest power plant. If the closest power plant is depleted, it consumes from the next closest plant.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
