/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (Economic activity is allocated to target nodes based on where people live, rather than where production occurs. Industrial zones, factories, and logistics hubs often generate significant GDP without corresponding resident populations, and these are underrepresented in the spatial distribution of demand.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (GDP values are treated as fixed, average quantities. In reality, economic activity varies daily and seasonally, and may change significantly over years.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (Relevance: A fixed GDP baseline is sufficient for long-term average risk assessment and comparison across regions. The model is not intended to capture short-term economic shocks or seasonal demand variation.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
281 0 obj
<<
