282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (Transmission lines are inferred using satellite-based nighttime light data and established open-source methodologies \(Arderne, Zorn, Nicolas, et al., 2020\). As the network is predicted rather than fully observed, spatial inaccuracies and missing lines may occur. These misalignments are a known trade-off in global and national-scale infrastructure modelling.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
283 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (Relevance: While unsuitable for granular investment decisions \(ie. a particular stretch of transmission line\) , the inferred network is sufficiently accurate for national-scale analysis where relative exposure and connectivity patterns are the primary concern. TF is aware that the model works in larger scales, and can advise on areas as a whole which are more or less vulnerable. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 757 0 R
/E ( In reality, electricity demand is dynamic, and met by a combination of sources distributed across the grid, the supply of which is also dynamic \(Enbridge, 2024\). However, the base methodology did not account for this dynamism, so our model is static, assuming constant values. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
285 0 obj
<<
