306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 143 0 R
/E (Hydropower assets are particularly sensitive to climate variability because their performance depends directly on hydrological conditions\(Opperman et al, 2023\). However, the mechanisms through which climate hazards affect generation differ substantially depending on plant type \(run-of-river versus reservoir-based\), location and hazard type. Hydropower plants generate electricity by converting river flows into energy, either instantaneously in run-of-river systems or through regulated storage in reservoir-based systems, implying fundamentally different exposure pathways to hydrological hazards \(REPSOL,2023\). As a result, a one-size-fits-all risk metric is not appropriate.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
