/E (Floods impact dam-type hydropower projects differently to run-off-river systems. For dams, the critical risks are overflowing and foundation defects \(cracks in the dam\) which account for roughly 85% of dam failures globally.\(ASDS, 2020\) Run-off-river systems lack buffers provided by reservoirs so are more likely to experience downtime due to floods with main risks being flash floods and increased debris flows. These differences require different approaches. )
