/P 146 0 R
/E (Using SPEI-based drought frequency, generation losses remain non-zero even when annual precipitation is above baseline, capturing the importance of intra-annual drought timing. Run-of-river plants \(Bugoye and Nyamwamba II\) exhibit similarly high losses, reflecting both their limited buffering capacity and their close geographic proximity, which exposes them to comparable drought conditions. In contrast, the reservoir plant \(Kikagati\) is less affected.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [11]
>>
