<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 157 0 R
/E (*The b scaling exponent demonstrates sensitivity to flooding. A lower b \(below 1.5\) means that sediment increases linearly with flood size and the sediment transport is dominated by frequent moderate floods. A higher b value means that sediment is dominated by rarer extreme floods, higher intensity causing more damage per-event. If the area has many flashy storms and landslide-prone areas a higher b is realistic. )
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
endobj
